.bmad-loop/cache/
.bmad-loop/policy.toml

# Historical story evidence logs are durable inputs. The `[Ll]ogs/` and `*.log`
# rules above silently excluded them, so evidence receipts bound maintainer acceptance to files that
# were never committed and would vanish on `git clean -xdf` (found in the Story 2.12 code review,
# 2026-07-28). These negations must stay after the `[Ll]ogs/` and `*.log` rules they override —
# the last matching pattern wins, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is still
# excluded, so the directory is re-included first. Only the selected Story 3.13
# packet negations are final, so generated evidence packages stay ignored.
#
# Corrected 2026-07-28 (delta code review). The first version was both too narrow and too broad:
#   too narrow — it matched only a lowercase `logs/` directory under `implementation-artifacts`, so
#                `evidence/<sha>/run.log` (a log beside the receipt rather than inside `logs/`),
#                `evidence/<sha>/Logs/run.log`, and anything under `planning-artifacts/evidence/`
#                were all still silently excluded. That is the same defect class this fix exists to
#                close.
#   too broad  — `!…/logs/**` re-included *everything* beneath an evidence `logs/` directory,
#                including `.dll` and `.nupkg` build output, which `git add -A` would then track.
# Re-include the directory first (git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded),
# then re-include only the log files themselves.
!_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/[Ll]ogs/
!_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.log
_bmad/render/


# OQ8 consumer validation virtualenv created by the documented source-only
# handoff bootstrap (python3 -m venv .oq8-python).
.oq8-python/

# Story 3.13 selected-packet archives are tracked evidence, not restore output.
# ValidatePackageBytes rehashes the 14 on-disk *.nupkg files. The *.nupkg rule
# ignores the archives themselves. **/[Pp]ackages/* ignores children of a
# packages/ directory, not the directory. Still re-include the directory first,
# then the archives, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded. Do not use !…/logs/** — that re-included build nupkgs in
# 2026-07-28. Generated evidence packages stay ignored. The selected Story 3.13
# packet is re-included after these rules.

# Story 3.22: new generated evidence belongs in external storage. These rules
# follow the legacy log negations. Final match ignores generated evidence
# packages. The selected Story 3.13 packet negations come last.
# Existing tracked evidence and source/snapshot baselines remain historical input.
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.zip
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.tar
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.tar.gz
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.tgz
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.7z
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.gz
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.xz
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.bz2
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.zst
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.rar
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.[0-9][0-9][0-9]
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.z[0-9][0-9]
# The split-volume patterns also match version-named directories such as
# sdk-10.0.400/; re-include directories only, so split archive files stay ignored.
!_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.[0-9][0-9][0-9]/
!_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.z[0-9][0-9]/
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.nupkg
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.part
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.part.*
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.webm
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.mp4
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.mov
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.avi
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.mkv
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.dmp
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.gcdump
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.etl
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.trace
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.nettrace
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/*.har
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/trace.dat
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/trace.json
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/traces/
_bmad-output/**/evidence/**/trace/
